","Rehearse","Melody","Year 1","E","F","F","F","G","Auto","Rehearse","Riley","Year 2","B","C","C","C","C","Auto","Rehearse","Saxophone","4 players","Rehearse 4","Choose for the whole Saxophone section","Paige","Year 3","B","B","B","B","C","Auto","Rehearse","Melody","Year 2","B","C","C","C","C","Auto","Rehearse","Adam","Year 3","A","A","A","A","C","Auto","Rehearse","Amelia","Year 2","B","B","B","B","C","Auto","Rehearse","Horn","4 players","Rehearse 4","Choose for the whole Horn section","Chloe","Year 3","C","C","C","C","C","Auto","Rehearse","Belle","Year 1","F","F","F","F","F","Auto","Rehearse","Henry","Year 2","B","C","C","C","C","Auto","Rehearse","Ben","Year 2","F","G","E","F","G","Auto","Rehearse","Trumpet","4 players","Rehearse 4","Choose for the whole Trumpet section","Anna","Year 3","S","S","A","A","C","Auto","Rehearse","Ryan","Year 1","G","G","G","G","G","Auto","Rehearse","Alex","Year 1","G","G","G","G","G","Auto","Rehearse","Max","Year 3","C","C","C","C","C","Auto","Rehearse","Trombone","3 players","Rehearse 3","Choose for the whole Trombone section","Lucy","Year 2","B","C","C","C","C","Auto","Rehearse","Elise","Year 2","E","E","F","E","F","Auto","Rehearse","Paige","Year 3","A","A","A","A","C","Auto","Rehearse","Low voices","5 players","Rehearse 5","Choose for the whole Low voices section","Summer","Year 3","S","A","A","A","C","Auto","Rehearse","Claire","Year 1","F","E","F","F","F","Auto","Rehearse","Finn","Year 2","B","C","C","C","C","Auto","Rehearse","Liam","Year 2","D","E","D","E","E","Auto","Rehearse","Melody","Year 3","B","B","A","A","C","Auto","Rehearse","Percussion","4 players","Rehearse 4","Choose for the whole Percussion section","Alice","Year 3","C","C","C","B","C","Auto","Rehearse","Alex","Year 3","B","A","B","A","C","Auto","Rehearse","Skye","Year 2","B","B","B","B","C","Auto","Rehearse","Adam","Year 1","G","G","G","G","G","Auto","Rehearse","This week's plan: Rehearse 39 players","Practice one week","Advance to next event","Tune by ear","Once a week, play the tuner's tone alongside a member's note. Adjust the pitch until the beats disappear. This improves that player's pitch.","Band skills","39 players / 39 seats","Pitch","D","Rhythm","D","Tone","D","Expr.","D","Togetherness","C","Free-piece reading","E","Set-piece reading","E","Stamina","56","Motivation","77","Venue experience","0","Reputation","53","More students want to join once reputation passes 58","Your coaching","Lv3","Trusted by the band · Practice benefit +10%","Average player skill","D","This time last year","E","This year","Last year","Prefecturals","April","May","June","July","August","September","October","Current performance review","Music room · Can-Can","Pitch","53","Rhythm","65","Tone","64","Cracked notes: 32","Expr.","43","Balance","65","The playing was accurate, but the music felt flat. Agree together on where each phrase should peak. The parts are not fully learned yet. There are 294 wrong notes.","Review practice","Reading","Pitch","Rhythm","Tone","Expr.","?","Adam Rogers","Year 1 · Crash cymbals","G","Alex Graham","Year 1 · Trumpet","G","Ben Scott","Year 2 · Horn","G","About this app","School Band Story · Version 1.0 · © Yu Studio","Privacy policy","Updated November 1, 2026 · Operator: Yu Studio","Your progress stays on your device. There are no ads, tracking or accounts.","Scope and operator","Yu Studio explains how information is handled in the iPhone, iPad and web versions of School Band Story.","In-game information","Member names, including edited names, practice, results, performance records, settings and introductory-guide progress are stored on your device so you can continue playing. They are not automatically sent to a developer server. The game does not obtain your real name, address, location or advertising identifiers, and includes no advertising, analytics or tracking SDKs.","Performances and device features","A recording is a record of a performance generated by the game. It does not record voices or ambient sound through the microphone. The app does not request access to your camera, microphone, contacts or location.","Storage, backups and deletion","The app stores progress in web storage and a backup within the app. Depending on device settings, it may be included in an operating-system backup. There is no separate cloud sync. The web version saves in your browser.","To remove app data, use Delete App in iOS Settings. Offload App keeps data. For the web version, remove the site's browser data. Operating-system backups, exported files and copies sent elsewhere must be deleted separately. Restoring a backup may restore the data.","When you export or share","Exporting a save or saving a performance creates a file on your device; you choose where to save or share it. Saves contain member names and play records. Audio files may include school names and school-year information. The service you choose has its own terms. Clipboard copying happens only when you request it.","When a connection is used","The app's game and this information are bundled and work offline. If you open an external website or email link, your browser or email app may connect to the internet.","The web game and public support pages require a connection. GitHub Pages, the host, handles connection information such as IP addresses. See","GitHub's privacy statement","for details. We do not add our own analytics or advertising cookies.","Support information","Email addresses, message text and attachments you send are used to answer inquiries and investigate problems. Gmail is used to send, receive and store email. Information is kept as long as needed for support and deleted when no longer needed. Except where required by law, it is not used for advertising or given to third parties without consent. Contact us below about deletion or other requests. You do not have to send your real name or save file.","Children and policy changes","The game does not obtain ages or collect information from children. Consult a parent or guardian before including personal information in an inquiry. If our handling of information changes, we will update this page and the in-app information.","Contact","Operator: Yu Studio","Email:","hy218355@gmail.com","Terms of use","Updated November 1, 2026 · Operator: Yu Studio","Information about using the game and keeping your data safe.","Scope","These terms apply to School Band Story provided by Yu Studio. Apps obtained from the App Store are also covered by Apple's Standard End User License Agreement. This information does not replace it with a custom EULA.","Apple's Standard EULA · external website","。","Playing and costs","There are no accounts, in-app purchases or advertisements. The app can be played offline. You are responsible for connection costs when using the web version, email, external websites or file-sharing services.","Rights in the game and its materials","Rights in the program, text, original images and other content belong to the operator or the respective rights holders. Materials are identified under Credits and licenses, and their use is governed by those licenses. Schools, characters and events are fictional. They do not depict actual people or schools, and the game does not guarantee real-world musical instruction or judging results.","Sharing gameplay and performances","You may share your gameplay screens, videos and exported performances in accordance with applicable law and the materials' licenses. Respect others' personal information and rights, and do not imply your content is an official release. When publishing performances containing Weresax samples, include the creator, source and CC BY 3.0 attribution shown in the credits.","Please avoid","Do not infringe laws or others' rights, distribute malicious programs, impersonate someone in an inquiry, or interfere with the operator or distribution services.","Protecting your data","Progress is stored on your device. It may be lost through deletion, device failure or clearing browser data. Periodically keep a separate copy using Export and import saves in the journal. Operation on every device and recovery of data cannot be guaranteed.","Updates and responsibility","Features, display and content may change through bug fixes and other updates. Important changes will be announced in the app or support pages. These terms do not exclude liability for the operator's intent or gross negligence, or liability that cannot legally be excluded or limited, including under Japan's Consumer Contract Act. They do not restrict statutory user rights.","Governing law and contact","These terms are interpreted under Japanese law. For questions, contact Yu Studio (","hy218355@gmail.com","). Please see the privacy policy for information handling.","Support and contact","Updated November 1, 2026 · Operator: Yu Studio","Troubleshooting and contact details.","Contact","Operator: Yu Studio","Email:","hy218355@gmail.com","Please tell us your device, OS version, what happened and what you did immediately beforehand, as far as you know. Your real name and save file are not required. Avoid including personal information in screenshots. Replies may take time. Email requires a configured email app and a connection.","No sound or quiet sound","Check your device and headphone volume and the output device, including Bluetooth. The app plays audio even in silent mode. Try Retry if it appears in Rehearse. If needed, stop playback and reopen the app.","Playback stopped during a call or in another app","Return to the app and check playback. If audio does not resume, stop and play again. Automatic locking is suppressed during playback, but manual locking or phone calls may stop the sound.","Changing devices and keeping saves","Export a save file from the journal and import it on the new device. Import replaces the current save, so keep a backup first. An OS backup may restore data, but manual export is recommended for a reliable transfer. The web and app versions do not sync automatically.","Exporting a performance","Use Save on a performance result or in the rehearsal recording library. The app normally exports m4a, or WAV if conversion fails. The web version exports WAV. Choose a destination in the share sheet. This does not record through the microphone.","Deleting data","Use Delete App in iOS Settings, or clear site data for the web version. Export any saves you need first. Manage exported files and operating-system backups separately. Starting a new band does not clear display settings and similar preferences.","Costs and connections","There are no in-app purchases, advertisements or accounts. The app includes all pieces and instrument samples. Email, external websites and chosen sharing services may use a connection.","Credits and licenses","Updated November 1, 2026 · Operator: Yu Studio","Sources for the music, instrument samples, artwork and fonts.","Music","Original works: Dvořák's New World Symphony, second movement; Beethoven's Ode to Joy; Offenbach's Orpheus in the Underworld; Elgar's Pomp and Circumstance; Verdi's Triumphal March; Handel's See, the Conqu'ring Hero Comes; Holst's Jupiter; Brahms's Hungarian Dance No. 5; Tchaikovsky's Waltz of the Flowers and Swan Lake Scene; Rossini's William Tell Overture; Bizet's Carmen Prelude; Wagner's Ride of the Valkyries; Vivaldi's Spring; and Pachelbel's Canon. They were arranged for this game's wind band from public-domain full scores, with some reference to PDMX (CC0). Performances are generated on the device according to the members' abilities.","Instrument samples","Versilian Studios' VSCO 2 Community Edition and VCSL, and Karoryfer Samples' Bear Sax use CC0 1.0. University of Iowa Electronic Music Studios Musical Instrument Samples are used under the unrestricted-use statement on that website.","VSCO 2 CE","／","VCSL","／","Bear Sax","／","University of Iowa","。","Selected notes have been trimmed, converted to mono, aligned, level-adjusted and looped. Some pitches are interpolated. Euphonium uses processed trombone samples.","Weresax · alto saxophone","Karoryfer Samples「Weresax」。","tonejs-instruments","Samples are used, following the repository's attribution, under","Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported（CC BY 3.0）",". They have been trimmed, converted to mono, aligned, level-adjusted and looped. This does not imply the creator endorses this game.","Example attribution: Weresax — Karoryfer Samples / via tonejs-instruments / CC BY 3.0 / samples modified.","Venue acoustics and sound effects","Venue reverberation was calculated with pyroomacoustics (MIT License) from room dimensions and materials. The library itself is not included in the app. Applause and some sound effects were synthesized for this game.","Art and icons","The 100 member candidates, Ms. Asano and the music room are fictional images made for this game using image-generation tools. The app icon, instruments and interface icons are original artwork. Images from other works were not used as source materials.","Fonts","Zen Kaku Gothic New, Klee One, Dela Gothic One and Share Tech Mono are bundled under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 and subset to the characters used. Copyright notices and the full licenses follow.","OFL-delagothicone.txt","OFL-kleeone.txt","OFL-sharetechmono.txt","OFL-zenkakugothicnew.txt","Band journal","May · Week 2","→ Miles Long・Anna Carter・Summer Young returned after exchanging contact details with students from the other school.  (Miles Long Pitch+1.5 Rhythm+1.0 / Anna Carter Pitch+1.5 Rhythm+1.0 / Summer Young Pitch+1.5 Rhythm+1.0)","[Joint section practice] A nearby high school invited members to a joint section practice. Up to three can go.","May · Week 1","→ Play long tones together. You played long tones together for a while. Before leaving, Skye Cox said, “I'll be back tomorrow.” (Band Stamina −3 / Skye Cox Pitch+2.0 Tone+4.0)","This week's practice: Long tones 11 players · Tuning 11 players · Metronome 1 player · Phrase practice 6 players · Piece practice 10 players. Band average Tone+6.2　Pitch+4.8　Rhythm+5.8　Expr.+6.6","Event: After practice, first-year Skye Cox (Clarinet) stayed in the music room. “I can't play like everyone else… Maybe I'm not suited to this.”","[Golden Week practice day] A full day of practice. Benefits are 1.5×, but stamina costs rise too.","April · Week 4","This week's practice: Piece practice. Band average Rhythm+2.0　Expr.+1.9　Pitch+1.0","Recorded the first rehearsal with the new members.","Assigned instruments to 10 new members. 4 got their first choice.","[New members and instruments] The first years have officially joined. Assign their instruments. Their preferred instruments boost motivation.","April · Week 3","→ Teach them the gestures. They practiced making the beat points clear. The section's entrances began to line up. (Band Togetherness+3 / Ruby Moore Rhythm+2.0)","This week's practice: Rehearse. Band average Pitch+1.6　Rhythm+1.8　Tone+1.6　Expr.+1.8","Event: Student conductor Ruby Moore asked, “I'd like to try conducting section practice. Could you watch?”","[Trial visits] First years visited the music room. Being the older members gave everyone a boost.","April · Week 2","Chloe Morgan was overwhelmed by performance nerves.","The band's reputation rose (51 → 53).","Welcome concert: Applause was scattered, but 10 first years seemed interested. Some students' eyes lit up at the sight of Clarinet and low voices.","Through performance experience, Ella Roberts learned Stage confidence○. Handles performance nerves well.","[Welcome concert] Introduce the band in the gym. The performance affects how many first years join. Students are more likely to want the instruments you showcase.","April · Week 1","The members now discuss where each phrase should peak.","Players are starting to sustain long notes right to the end.","The beats between unison notes are slowing down.","Attacks are becoming steadier. Fewer notes crack.","This week's practice: Rehearse. Band average Pitch+1.5　Rhythm+1.9　Tone+1.6　Expr.+1.8","Chose Verdi · Triumphal March from Aida as the set piece.","With at least 15 members, the band enters Division A. A set piece and free piece open the path to regionals and nationals.","Chose Offenbach · Infernal Galop from Orpheus in the Underworld as the free piece and recorded the first rehearsal.","Assigned instruments to 2 new members. 2 got their first choice.","School year 2028 has begun, with 27 members. Choose a free piece.","2027 October · Week 3","Graduation. The first and second years played a farewell for Ava Simmons.","Entered the Ensemble Contest with 5 players from Anna Carter・Max Reed・Ruby Moore・Miles Long・Summer Young. Silver. (83.8 points)","The band's reputation rose (55 → 56).","Winter plan: Build fundamentals. Keep up long tones and scales through winter, developing each member's weaker skills..","1 third years retired, and a new band of 27 first and second years began. Miles Long is the new band captain.","After the annual concert, 1 third years retired.","After hearing the performance, Year 1: Ben Scott、Year 1: Elise Morris came to the music room. “I want to join too.”","The band's reputation rose (46 → 55).","Annual concert · third years' farewell: Applause from the full hall seemed to last forever. The third years' eyes were red.","[Annual concert · third years' farewell] The third years' final performance. Families, graduates and neighbors gather at Civic Hall.","2027 October · Week 2","This week's practice: Rehearse. Band average Pitch+2.0　Rhythm+2.2　Tone+2.0　Expr.+2.2","→ Have one last rehearsal with the third years. The final note lingered in the music room like a hall's reverberation. No one lowered their instrument right away. (Band Reading +1)","Event: The week before the annual concert, third-year Ava Simmons and the others were passing their marked parts and practice notebooks to younger members.","2027 October · Week 1","Chat: Adam Nelson (Tenor sax) asked, “I'd like a part-time job. Could I miss practice once a week?”","This week's practice: Tuning 1 player · Phrase practice 2 players · Rest 25 players. Band average Expr.+9.9　Pitch+7.9　Tone+1.1","→ Once a week is fine. Adam looked relieved. They practice more intently on the other days.","2027 September · Week 4","→ Miles Long filled the part with notes about what they had learned.  (Miles Long Pitch+4.0)","This week's practice: Rehearse. Band average Pitch+2.2　Rhythm+2.4　Tone+2.1　Expr.+2.5","[A short professional lesson] An instrument shop is offering a brief lesson with a professional. One member can attend.","Assigned instruments to Liam Wood. 1 got their first choice.","2027 September · Week 3","After hearing the performance, Year 1: Liam Wood came to the music room. “I want to join too.”","The band's reputation rose (40 → 46).","School festival: Families and classmates offered warm applause.","Miles Long、Adam Nelson、Chloe Wood、Zoe Roberts played above their usual level.","[School festival] Take the gym stage at the school festival. Classmates and families come to listen.","2027 September · Week 2","Chloe Morgan shared their feelings with Sophie Graham, but was turned down.","Paige Turner's dream came true: Play as well as an older member I admire. Next dream: Learn two skills.","This week's practice: Rehearse 26 players · Rest 1 player. Band average Pitch+2.2　Rhythm+2.6　Tone+2.2　Expr.+2.4","→ That care will show in your sound, too. Looking pleased, Riley began long tones on the gleaming instrument. (Riley Ford Tone growth +6%)","Chat: Riley Ford (Flute) seems to love polishing their instrument. “I lose track of time.”","2027 September · Week 1","Miles Long's dream came true: Overcome my performance nerves. Next dream: Reach regionals.","This week's practice: Rehearse. Band average Pitch+2.2　Rhythm+2.5　Tone+2.2　Expr.+2.6","→ Let them take it easy this week. Max Reed spent the week studying the part, singing while moving their fingers. (Band Motivation+1 · Reading +1 / Max Reed Tone−1.0)","Event: Max Reed (Trumpet) seems to have hurt their lips. High notes are painful.","The band decided to revisit the competition piece, Can-Can, at the annual concert.","2027 August · Week 4","Summer break ended and the second term began.","2027 August · Week 1","Adam Nelson played above their usual level.","The competition season is over. the third years' final performance: the annual concert in October · Week 3.","Competition reserves will rejoin everyone in autumn.","Rival Tsukimidai High School: Gold (average 85.5). Not there yet.","The band's reputation rose (37 → 40).","Prefecturals (Division A) result: Silver (Set piece 62.3 · Free piece 65.7)。","Coaching rose to Lv3 (Trusted by the band). Practice benefits are now +10%.","The week of Band Competition · Prefecturals has arrived.","2027 July · Week 4","The week before Event: Band Competition · Prefecturals, captain Ava Simmons asked, “Please, could we play through it once more?”","This week's practice: Venue rehearsal 6 players · Rest 21 players. Band average Pitch+0.5　Rhythm+0.4　Tone+0.5　Expr.+0.6","→ Let them play through before leaving. After the last note, everyone packed away in silence. They looked ready. (Band Togetherness+2 Stamina −6 · Reading +3)","2027 July · Week 3","→ Have them rest this week. You explained that rest is part of practice. The following week, Ava Simmons unpacked their instrument looking refreshed. (Band Motivation+1 Stamina +1)","This week's practice: Rehearse 22 players · Rest 5 players. Band average Pitch+4.0　Rhythm+4.6　Tone+4.1　Expr.+4.9","Event: Ava Simmons (E♭ clarinet) looks pale. They seem to be practicing late into the night at home.","[Summer camp · second half] The second half of camp. Fatigue builds, but the ensemble is coming together.","Getting started with Ms. Asano","Start over","Sections and members","?","All years","Year 1","Year 2","Year 3","All instruments","39 / 39 players","Section overview","Flute","4/4 players","B","B","B","B","Double reeds","2/2 players","B","B","A","B","Clarinet","9/9 players","E","